# {{PROJECT_NAME}}

Laravel 12 app sold in tiers: {{TIERS_LABEL}}. Core ({{CORE_TIER_LABEL}}) lives in `app/`; each
higher tier is a module in `modules/<Tier>/`. A client release contains only the tiers that
client has, because `scripts/build-release.sh` removes the rest from the code.

## Getting started

```bash
composer install
cp .env.example .env
php artisan key:generate
php artisan migrate
php artisan serve
```

## Tiers

- `{{PREFIX_UPPER}}_TIER` in `.env` picks the active tier. Development defaults to `{{TOP_TIER}}`.
- `php artisan {{PREFIX}}:feature` lists feature switches; add a name and `--on`, `--off` or
  `--reset` to change one.
- Check permissions in views with `<x-can permission="...">`, and render menus with
  `<x-menu section="main" />`.
- Core never references `Modules\`. `tests/Feature/ArchTest.php` enforces it.

Run the suite at every tier before committing:

```bash
for tier in {{TIERS_SPACED}}; do {{PREFIX_UPPER}}_TIER=$tier php artisan test || break; done
```

## Releases

```bash
scripts/build-release.sh <tier> <version>    # e.g. scripts/build-release.sh {{CORE_TIER}} 1.0.0
```

The script writes a fresh one-commit repo and a zip to `../<project>-releases/` and prints the SHA-256.
Paths that never ship are listed in `release.exclude`.

## AI agents

`AGENTS.md` has the rules for coding agents, including the commit review gate. A human approves
every commit; `scripts/propose-commit.sh` asks for that approval on the terminal.
